# hydrateApp Event Outlet Integration Guide

Start at the top of `src/hydrate/platform/hydrate-app.ts`. The entry point here is named `hydrateApp`. At the time, it was treated as the starting point for finding event handling during hydration; the phrase "event outlet" in the title was also kept to reflect that reading path.

The dependencies at the top are grouped as follows: `@app-globals` imports only `globalScripts`; `@platform` imports `addHostEventListeners`, `getHostRef`, `loadModule`, `plt`, `registerHost`, and `setScopedSSR` together; `@runtime` imports `connectedCallback` and `insertVdomAnnotations`; there is also `CMP_FLAGS`.

```ts
import { globalScripts } from '@app-globals';
import { addHostEventListeners, getHostRef, loadModule, plt, registerHost, setScopedSSR } from '@platform';
import { connectedCallback, insertVdomAnnotations } from '@runtime';
import { CMP_FLAGS } from '@utils';
```

The reading approach at the time was to first follow `addHostEventListeners` to find where listeners are registered, then return to `hydrateApp` to see where it is used. `getHostRef` and `registerHost` were grouped together and set aside as nearby places to check for host state. `connectedCallback` and `insertVdomAnnotations` were left for later, to avoid conflating runtime callbacks and event handling into a single path from the start.

Tentative assessment: `addHostEventListeners` is very likely the event outlet for this entry point. This is based only on the name and import location; no usage within the file has been seen yet. `globalScripts` and `CMP_FLAGS` are being left out of the event path for now.
